# KNOWN GAP — a single-owner value arriving as a BARE PARAMETER cannot be
# boxed, and the compiler now REFUSES to mint rather than minting a wrong box.
#
#     Box[Box[String]] wrap(Box[String] s):
#         return Box[Box[String]](s)
#
# `s` is a `Box[String]` param, so it arrives as a POINTER. The ownership
# boundary asks `ptr_materialization_kind` what to do with it and gets
# `PassThrough`: `Box[T]` is a single-owner carve-out with no clone fn, so
# there is no owning representation to materialize into. The operand therefore
# survives the boundary STILL POINTER-TYPED, and the mint has no C name for a
# pointer — it would fall to its residue arm and mint `Box__int64_t`, the same
# element-type collapse `tests/fixtures/box_ctor_primitive_element_types.gg`
# pins for primitives, reached by a route no primitive fixture can see.
#
# ⚠ THIS IS A REAL PROGRAM, NOT A CONSTRUCTED IMPOSSIBILITY. It builds today
# and it does the wrong thing: before the refusal it built rc 0 and SEGV'd at
# `rc 139` on the deref; with the collapse un-refused it built rc 0 and printed
# `(null)`. A crash converted into a silent wrong answer is worse, not better.
#
# ⛔ THE REFUSAL IS A LOWERING-LAYER STOPGAP, cited to `todo/t0682`. The
# reference-grade rejection is a `gg check` diagnostic — `E_MoveWithoutOperator`
# at constructor positions and for field sources — in `src/semantic/safety/`.
# `gg check` on this program is rc 0 TODAY, which is exactly `t0682`. When
# `t0682` lands, this program is rejected before lowering and the mint's
# `panic!` becomes an unreachable backstop; this fixture then moves to a
# `check_gg_fails` assertion and out of `known_gaps/`.
#
# ⊕ ALSO LIVE AND SEPARATELY FILED (`todo/t1077`): writing the move the
# diagnostic would ask for — `^` at the parameter and at the ctor — does NOT
# rescue the program. Nested `Box[Box[T]]` is broken independently of the
# ownership question.
#
# EXPECTED (today, and asserted by the LIVE test that cites this file):
#   `gg build` FAILS, naming the refusal and citing `todo/t0680`.
# EXPECTED (once `todo/t0682` lands):
#   `gg check` FAILS with `E_MoveWithoutOperator`.

from std.collections import Box

String mk(String a, String b):
    return a + b

Box[Box[String]] wrap(Box[String] s):
    return Box[Box[String]](s)

void main():
    Box[String] b = Box[String](mk("aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa", "bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb"))
    Box[Box[String]] w = wrap(b)
    print((*(*w)))
